The try-throw-catch block
❑The try-throw-catch block is written as follows:
try {
  Code to run;
  A statement or method that may throw an exception;
  More code to run;
}
catch (type ex) {
  Code to process the exception;
}
❑An exception may be thrown directly using a throw statement in a 
try block, or indirectly by a method that may throw an exception.

