slides.raw_text:
Catching Exceptions
❑When an exception is thrown, it can be caught and handled 
in a try-catch block, as follows:
If no exceptions arise during the 
execution of the try block, the 
catch blocks are skipped.
If one statement inside the try 
block throws an exception, the 
remaining statements are skipped 
and the catch block that handles 
the exception is executed.
try {
  statements;  // statements may throw exceptions
}
catch (Exception1 ex1) {
  handler for exception1;
}
catch (Exception2 ex2) { 
  handler for exception2;
}
catch (ExceptionN exN) {
  handler for exceptionN;
}

